{"chunk_id": "8423ce75ea88", "text": "Kunti, having invoked the sun god Surya through a sacred mantra, finds herself unable to dismiss him when he appears and demands union. Torn between fear of his curse and the shame and social ruin that would follow if she obeyed him, she struggles internally with duty, reputation, and innocence. Surya argues that no sin will touch her and promises she will remain a virgin afterward; he also foretells that their son will be mighty and born with divine armor and earrings. Reluctantly consenting, Kunti receives Surya through his yogic power and faints. She later gives birth secretly to a radiant child\u2014Karna\u2014already bearing the celestial armor and earrings. Afraid of disgrace as an unmarried mother, she sorrowfully places the infant in a sealed basket and sets him afloat on the river, praying for his safety. The episode establishes Karna\u2019s divine origin and the tragic secrecy that shapes his fate.\nKunti, fearing Surya\u2019s curse and social shame, consents to him; he grants a son with divine armor and earrings while preserving her virginity.\nThemes: divine conception, honor and shame, female agency and constraint, divine boon, birth of Karna", "vector": [0.006155505310744047, -0.03217313438653946, 0.0013382998295128345, 0.0005237741279415786, -0.020293613895773888, 0.02467595599591732, -0.01762375794351101, -0.004250871948897839, -0.03799827769398689, -0.024608535692095757, 0.016423670575022697, 0.013726843520998955, 0.016801225021481514, 0.015304487198591232, -0.008056767284870148, -0.002779416274279356, 0.04964856430888176, -0.02125098742544651, 0.02706264704465866, -0.03570597618818283, -0.005555461160838604, -0.009688346646726131, -0.021480217576026917, 0.011576125398278236, -0.027777306735515594, 0.009236629121005535, 0.02204655110836029, -0.034735117107629776, 0.014778605662286282, -0.03384516388177872, -0.011791870929300785, 0.01047716848552227, -0.002386690815910697, -0.006010550539940596, -0.02665812335908